  "id": "Kingston-22_03507_HOU",
  "description": "Erection of a new detached garage and garden door access following demolition of existing detached garage",
  "decision_date": "28/12/2022",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced within 3 years from the date of this decision. \r\rReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act, 1990 (As amended)\r",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified on the approved plans and on the application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r",
    "Prior to occupation, a Fire Safety Strategy shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The Fire Safety Strategy shall demonstrate how the development will achieve the highest standards of fire safety and shall include the following details: 1) suitably positioned outside space for fire appliances/ an evacuation assembly point; 2) Appropriate fire alarm systems; 3) Passive and active fire safety measures; 4) appropriate construction details to minimise the risk of fire spread; 5) provision of suitable and convenient means of escape/ an evacuation strategy; 6) provision of suitable access and equipment for firefighting which is appropriate for the size and use of the development. The Fire safety Strategy shall include a statement of competence.\r\rThe development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved strategy prior to occupation and thereafter maintained.\r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users in accordance with Policy D12 (Fire safety) of the London Plan 2021. \r",
    "The garage hereby permitted shall only be used as domestic ancillary purposes in connection to the main house at No. 85 Malden Hill, New Malden and shall not be used for commercial operations or storage  without the grant of further specific planning permission from the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To safeguard the character and appearance of the suburban residential context of the area and the amenity of neighbouring occupiers, and to prevent the intensification of the site. \r"
  ],
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments"
